<title>FRANCE: Traders detail Saudi barley deliveries.</title>
<headline>Traders detail Saudi barley deliveries.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Some two-thirds of the one million tonnes of barley bought by Saudi Arabia on Thursday will be delivered in September and the rest in October, traders said.</p>
<p>The deal is for 400,000 tonnes of barley to be supplied to the Red Sea port of Jeddah, and 200,000 tonnes to the east coast port of Dammam, in September.</p>
<p>October's deliveries of 400,000 tonnes will be split between 300,000 tonnes arriving at Jeddah and 100,000 tonnes at Dammam.</p>
</text>
